// Tests the relation OffloadPropagateGridCoverage records between a launch
// grid dimension and a kernel argument.
//
// The Y and Z dimensions matter for loops strided over the grid extent alone
// (`for (j = blockIdx.y; j < n; j += gridDim.y)`).  Establishing
// gridDim.y >= n bounds the trip count at 1 so the loop can fold away.  The
// fact is recorded as dim/argument/divisor triples.
//
// A clamped extent, the usual spelling of the per-dimension launch limit, must
// not produce the fact: on a launch where the clamp bit, the grid no longer
// covers the argument and the loop really does iterate.  (The pass can instead
// emit a guarded clone carrying the fact, but that is off by default.)

// RUN: cir-opt --split-input-file --cir-offload-tighten-launch-bounds \
// RUN:         --cir-offload-propagate-grid-coverage %s | FileCheck %s

// gridDim.y is exactly ne01 (argument 2), so the relation holds with divisor 1.
// The fact belongs on the clone the launch was redirected to, not the original.
// CHECK: cir.offload.func @_Z1kPfii$max256
// CHECK-SAME: grid_covers_dims = array<i32: 1, 2, 1>

!s32i = !cir.int<s, 32>
!s64i = !cir.int<s, 64>
!u32i = !cir.int<u, 32>
!u8i = !cir.int<u, 8>
!void = !cir.void
!rec_dim3 = !cir.struct<"dim3" {!u32i, !u32i, !u32i}>
